# Board viewport layout and scale

Refine both fixed zoom levels and allow Detail panning beneath persistent Board controls.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Detail uses a visibly higher fixed zoom level than the current implementation.
- [x] Detail panning can move board content behind Done, edit controls, help, and player selection.
- [x] Persistent controls remain fixed, visually above the board, fully legible, and interactive.
- [x] Pan bounds still prevent losing the board entirely and permit reaching every playable edge and vertex.
- [x] Overview shifts slightly upward and appears visually centred in the complete screen layout.
- [x] View and edit modes share consistent board geometry without jumping when mode changes.
- [x] Tap-to-focus, long-hold radial editing, and immediate Detail pan arbitration remain unchanged.
- [x] Deterministic viewport and UI regression bundles compile.
- [ ] Focused gesture/layout checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- Keep the two-level discrete pinch model; continuous zoom is not requested.

## Evidence

- Increased fixed Detail scale from 1.65 to 1.85 and expanded bounded pan travel from 45% to 55% of the viewport dimensions.
- Added a deterministic Overview display offset of 3.5% upward while Detail uses its stored bounded pan offset.
- Rebuilt `BoardScreen` as a full-area Board ZStack with fixed controls overlaid above it; edit/view mode no longer changes Board geometry.
- Extended viewport tests for the new scale, bounds, Overview bias, and Detail display offset.
- The complete app and test bundles compile using `/private/tmp/Catanalyst-tasks018-024-derived`.
